                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4e23fce7-cae9-45fd-9d79-674d25dec42b",
                        "entry_id": "1c404bf5-7e6e-3996-9d49-59c59215308f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "athéistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1fa378e1-3733-32d1-b93c-a7667c658b0c",
                        "entry_id": "1c404bf5-7e6e-3996-9d49-59c59215308f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à l’athéisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "451a6015-daab-4401-bc04-2089830ab0ba",
                                "sense_id": "1fa378e1-3733-32d1-b93c-a7667c658b0c",
                                "text": "Pendant des siècles, on avait compris (à tort) l’épicurisme comme une orientation strictement athéiste."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fc3e8bb-468f-4c14-a469-5d28cbdeb06b",
                                "sense_id": "1fa378e1-3733-32d1-b93c-a7667c658b0c",
                                "text": "Sa position n’est nullement athéiste : il croit trouver dans le discours le moyen de s’élever au-dessus de tout discours et d’atteindre l’absolu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7167505f-4ee2-3b4c-88da-4df9524572f3",
                        "entry_id": "1c404bf5-7e6e-3996-9d49-59c59215308f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(moderne) Qui n'est adepte ni d'une religion, ni d'une secte en isme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "519ada7f-7e81-3989-bdb2-c25ec3df4008",
                "word": "athéiste",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "751bb293-6182-41bc-ae00-e35610064252",
                        "entry_id": "519ada7f-7e81-3989-bdb2-c25ec3df4008",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "athéistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69608f75-c17d-3091-b6fd-85f65ebb6572",
                        "entry_id": "519ada7f-7e81-3989-bdb2-c25ec3df4008",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Athée, personne qui ne croit pas en l’existence d’un ou plusieurs dieux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d6c0620-a953-42d2-ac2c-d6e3a84ba08b",
                                "sense_id": "69608f75-c17d-3091-b6fd-85f65ebb6572",
                                "text": "Et sous le crime de lèse-majesté, les Ordonnances, avec l'intolérance barbare qui caractérise la législation de toute cette époque, comprennent « tous athéistes, libertins (c'est-à-dire ceux qui se sont affranchis des lois de la religion, soit pour la croyance, soit pour la pratique), anabaptistes et autres adhérents à sectes réprouvées par la censure commune, […]. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dab3ae75-f214-41a5-8dd5-078c920dab81",
                                "sense_id": "69608f75-c17d-3091-b6fd-85f65ebb6572",
                                "text": "Publiquement, le professeur Penrose Lucas est un auteur et un athéiste militant connu, qui a de plus en plus d’adeptes, poursuivit Brown."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "317b043a-c58d-4b12-8537-14e22d1cefd4",
                        "source_entry_id": "519ada7f-7e81-3989-bdb2-c25ec3df4008",
                        "source_sense_id": "69608f75-c17d-3091-b6fd-85f65ebb6572",
                        "target_lang_word": "Atheist",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Atheist",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                        "entry_id": "88b7c5b2-ae7f-3221-ad26-285a980cfd42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Person, welche die Existenz Gottes abstreitet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "596d8ec3-fa09-41a0-8b19-1c28958b2fd6",
                                                "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                                "text": "Atheisten glauben nicht an Gott."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e580b27e-92fd-4487-9d34-52fc8cbe4a8b",
                                                "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                                "text": "„Ich hatte zuvor nicht gewusst, dass wir in Ägypten so viele Atheisten haben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0eb98eb6-da2d-40bf-95cf-6d54ad7f0f6c",
                                                "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                                "text": "„Dass Michnik sich als Atheist bezeichnet, hilft ihm nicht.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d43b61ff-39b1-48fa-a5ff-9a9199741583",
                                                "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                                "text": "„Huxley wurde nicht deshalb ein so inbrünstiger Darwinianer, weil er an Darwins Theorie von der natürlichen Zuchtwahl geglaubt hätte – er hat ihr zu keinem Zeitpunkt Glauben geschenkt –, sondern weil Darwin gleich ihm ganz offensichtlich Atheist war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee8c358-8d46-4c5f-84bf-b981ae96e693",
                                                "sense_id": "70e26d1a-cc42-3bbd-b450-daa7d31f9003",
                                                "text": "„Zumra Nuru ist einer der wenigen Atheisten Äthiopiens und der wohl bekannteste Ungläubige seines Landes.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3762ebd2-aa8c-4732-812e-1516589d39fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "519ada7f-7e81-3989-bdb2-c25ec3df4008",
                        "source_sense_id": "69608f75-c17d-3091-b6fd-85f65ebb6572",
                        "target_lang_word": "atheist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "atheist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3be19f1b-af37-3cb4-80e4-86bbbe6333da",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in deities or gods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ba9b77e-5b64-4dcc-b265-7762e3aa0dba",
                                                "sense_id": "3be19f1b-af37-3cb4-80e4-86bbbe6333da",
                                                "text": "Atheists. One who does not believe in the existence of a Supreme Being, an atheist, is incompetent as a witness, being incapable of being sworn. […] Changed by Acts of 1851, No. 12 (P. S. 1593), under which, no question can be raised as to a witness's \"opinions on matters of religious belief.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46abe5e6-5ecf-309b-82c8-822fd3ea1e3f",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in deities or gods.",
                                            "A person who is certain that no deities exist or who thinks that the existence of deities can be disproven."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0664771a-4010-4327-a9a9-ec7b11ec9f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "46abe5e6-5ecf-309b-82c8-822fd3ea1e3f",
                                                "text": "Ageine, the Atheistes, which say in their hartes there is no God; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16284ee4-2992-4cd0-a74f-b4046fdc70cc",
                                                "sense_id": "46abe5e6-5ecf-309b-82c8-822fd3ea1e3f",
                                                "text": "An atheist, like a Christian, holds that we can know whether or not there is a God. The Christian holds that we can know there is a God; the atheist, that we can know there is not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7eddb7e9-0448-359c-9b15-282502e89fd2",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in deities or gods.",
                                            "A person who doubts the existence of deities (therefore, an agnostic may be considered an atheist)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "380e9895-64b8-46f3-9a3f-5a6539ae90b8",
                                                "sense_id": "7eddb7e9-0448-359c-9b15-282502e89fd2",
                                                "text": "Minister—Are you really an Atheist?\nAtheist—Yes.\nM.—Do you deny that there is a god?\nA.—No. I deny that there is sufficient reason to believe there is one. There may be a god, but I think it rather unlikely."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a78e368-ea3d-4700-b002-a3a49e5ec560",
                                                "sense_id": "7eddb7e9-0448-359c-9b15-282502e89fd2",
                                                "text": "Very low probability, but short of zero. De facto atheist. ‘I cannot know for certain but I think God is very improbable, and I live my life on the assumption that he is not there.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e051c41-be82-38bd-ad7f-b4523188897e",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in deities or gods.",
                                            "Any person lacking belief in deities (including children who are unaware of religion)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6120750c-ecc5-43aa-8784-b11f4dfe57ed",
                                                "sense_id": "5e051c41-be82-38bd-ad7f-b4523188897e",
                                                "text": "All children are born Atheists; they have no idea of God. Are they then criminal on account of their ignorance?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd3bad16-ebfe-3d01-b7eb-8bec02924ff0",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in a particular deity (but may believe in another deity)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fb5a508-c26a-46bd-986c-47f98d320d48",
                                                "sense_id": "dd3bad16-ebfe-3d01-b7eb-8bec02924ff0",
                                                "text": "Malice and prejudice concurred in representing the Christians as a society of atheists, who, by the most daring attack on the religious constitution of the empire, had merited the severest animadversion of the civil magistrate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3d9e26a-88b6-49aa-97d2-3a7064d5440f",
                                                "sense_id": "dd3bad16-ebfe-3d01-b7eb-8bec02924ff0",
                                                "text": "An atheist is just somebody who feels about Yahweh the way any decent Christian feels about Thor or Baal or the golden calf. As has been said before, we are all atheists about most of the gods that humanity has ever believed in. Some of us just go one god further."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdc9ac1b-4b43-46e6-b4a4-025c91e291e8",
                                                "sense_id": "dd3bad16-ebfe-3d01-b7eb-8bec02924ff0",
                                                "text": "Throughout history, atheists were simply people who did not believe the prevalent God of the day. For the sun-worshippers, Christians were atheists. For Jewish people, Christians were atheists. Whoever does not believe in your God is by definition, an atheist. […] With all the countless Gods concocted by man, I claim that my Christian friends and I have something in common. We are all atheists, I just believe in one less God than they."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                        "entry_id": "00665034-b7dc-37b1-96a3-c57e2a3d3b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does not believe in any religion (not even a religion without gods); a nonreligious person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe0db722-9e12-4e3b-8eb4-c8eaca8960fa",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "This is one of the strongest Grounds of Suspicion to me, and assures me that he has very little Regard to Religion in general; that he can pretend to marry you, and know nothing whether you are a Heathen or Christian; an Atheist or religious Person, a Papist or a Protestant; the Man can have no great Value for Religion, that is so little concerned whether his Wife has any, or no; for I take the Thing to weigh as much on one Side as on the other, where there is any serious Confideration at Bottom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea56c4df-5cd5-4fe8-aea0-2ed6483781bf",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "For instance, in Morocco, while a Muslim man is free to marry a non-Muslim woman, provided she is Christian or Jewish, but not Buddhist, Hindu or Atheist, a Muslim woman is only supposed to marry a Muslim man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b9666aa-096f-4f29-96f4-7367969d18b7",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "Since radio and TV started playing Atheists Like Me, the lead song in the album, Huang's record company has received more than 100 phone calls protesting the content of the new song, the local China Times newspaper reported.[…]\nIt's not clear who has been offended by the tune, but most Taiwanese are Buddhists or Daoists. A small number are Christians, Muslims and atheists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a86c9a9-8b53-4f2b-821f-6bbf4e36697c",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "In her chapter, “Freedom of and Freedom from Religion: Atheist Involvement in Legal Cases,” Lori G. Beaman presents her reflections on the various claims made by atheists in the legal arena, such as the objection to prayers in municipal[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776334c4-7e73-467f-8f8f-dd05bf5de41d",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "20 “We just need to get rid of religion,” atheist author and entertainer Penn Jillette has said. Many atheists agree, as you can tell from the popularity of antireligion books such as Christopher Hitchens's God Is Not Great."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6e47d58-8cab-4a7f-ab0d-a385ca7d636b",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "The legal image of the atheist constructed by these cases implies that the atheist or religious none is unworthy of voice and indeed of citizenship, that they are not part of the history of the nation, and that they are therefore unable to contribute to the public discussion about religion or its place in the public sphere."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "122c518e-611f-4716-b430-6e801a7fa2f6",
                                                "sense_id": "69097b86-baf0-323d-a15b-0e55fb7b5925",
                                                "text": "Moreover, we also know that an atheist or agnostic is statistically more likely to be autistic than neurotypical and a religious believer is statistically more likely to be neurotypical than autistic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "atheist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "000ecec9-2219-369f-b9ef-a1fd93b2aae6",
                                        "entry_id": "80fb7560-d319-33ec-9ae6-4fddac7eaa93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to atheists or atheism; atheistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77b8ea49-061c-43a4-9eb9-b97bf178b120",
                                                "sense_id": "000ecec9-2219-369f-b9ef-a1fd93b2aae6",
                                                "text": "He would have been seven times more Epicure and atheist than he was."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f4b37a-03b4-4eb4-8046-27c01670e8d4",
                                                "sense_id": "000ecec9-2219-369f-b9ef-a1fd93b2aae6",
                                                "text": "God! That majestic name is in the pledge. In doing this the government has already made clear that our country believes in God! We are the majority! Our nation is not Buddhist, not Hinduist, not Atheist, and the list goes on!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "atheist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2278090e-5729-3229-a45d-75ee2a85c3a4",
                                        "entry_id": "2533199f-8428-326f-b125-5fe358a3bccb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make someone an atheist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b9e5c60-5641-4c04-b8a8-039788c047a7",
                                                "sense_id": "2278090e-5729-3229-a45d-75ee2a85c3a4",
                                                "text": "The multitude of opinions doth draw him away, or else Atheist him, that he will be nothing. […] The multitude of opinions […] doth un-atheist him, put him upon the search and examination what is the truth of God."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
